GPUI Kit integrations and editor overlays
Sailry uses GPUI Kit 0.8.1 from https://github.com/dux-web/gpui-component at
4424427e60fcc9a95cd2a7daeacd77cc51b92e85 (Apache-2.0), based on official
https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit commit
18be16887bc2cb462f7b0a33c18bf6183344e7de. The maintained changes preserve
fullscreen dialogs, notifications above modal surfaces, caller-controlled tab
shrinking and minimum widths, and exact diff source while hiding optional
missing-newline labels. They retain the framework's current centering, safe
insets, focus, dismissal and native composition behavior.

All nine GPUI Fast packages use the immutable 0.1.12 release sources in
https://github.com/dux-web/gpui-fast at
82d917787a233f508ae06ef12a48518085c47297. Their archives match the official
Kit lockfile's registry checksums. The only production source change preserves
macOS NSView descendant hit testing before filtering the GPUI overlay itself,
from the previously reviewed compatibility source at
aa12fda8c18c5b8fb1a0b2ff16650cf138908b8b. The distribution retains upstream
Apache-2.0 licenses, original package manifests and provenance in its NOTICE.
GPUI WebView owns native composition on macOS with GPUI Fast. Upstream packages
retain their license files; Sailry's license copies remain in third_party_licenses/.

Russh RSA compatibility
The maintained russh 0.62.4 source at https://github.com/dux-web/russh.git,
commit c82704bff3b3c8d39676efc447b5e7db02ff29d3, retains the upstream
Apache-2.0 license from https://github.com/warp-tech/russh. It updates the RSA
and PKCS#1 constraints to 0.10.0-rc.19 and 0.8.0-rc.5 and uses the upstream
borrowed RsaPrivateKeyRef encoding type, with an ordinary key round-trip and
signature regression. Its original RSA and SSH features remain enabled.

